  "manualNoticeLabel": "Message shown in the app",
  "manualC01Title": "Getting started",
  "manualC01S1Heading": "Setup on first start",
  "manualC01S1B1": "On first start, WhisPaste guides you through the setup. You can go back to any step, and you can change everything later in Settings.",
  "manualC01S1B2I1": "Welcome: a short overview of WhisPaste.",
  "manualC01S1B2I2": "Privacy: what stays on your device.",
  "manualC01S1B2I3": "Speech model: choose the speech model and download it. If an API key for a cloud provider is already saved, you can choose that provider instead.",
  "manualC01S1B2I4": "Hotkey: set the key combination that starts a recording.",
  "manualC01S1B2I5": "Appearance: turn start at login on or off.",
  "manualC01S1B2I6": "{k1}: whether text is pasted automatically. On Linux, this step is skipped.",
  "@manualC01S1B2I6": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC01S1B2I7": "Try it: a test recording, then you are ready. Without a speech model or a chosen cloud provider with an API key, finishing stays locked.",
  "manualC01S2Heading": "System requirements",
  "manualC01S2B1": "WhisPaste needs a device with at least {ram} of memory (RAM). On devices with less, WhisPaste shows only a notice instead of the app.",
  "@manualC01S2B1": {
    "placeholders": {
      "ram": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC01S2B2": "You need a microphone to record. In onboarding you can continue without one, but you can only record once a microphone is connected.",
  "manualC01S3Heading": "Downloading a speech model",
  "manualC01S3B1": "WhisPaste turns your speech into text, either on your device or through a cloud provider with your own key. On your device it needs a model. You start the download yourself; it does not start automatically.",
  "manualC01S3B2I1": "Parakeet: fast, for European languages, about {k1}.",
  "@manualC01S3B2I1": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC01S3B2I2": "Whisper: all 99 languages, models from about {k1} to about {k2}.",
  "@manualC01S3B2I2": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k2": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC01S3B2I3": "The models are stored in the app’s data folder, in the {k1} subfolder.",
  "manualC01S3B4": "A Whisper model stays loaded after a recording, so the next start is faster. Under “Keep model loaded” in the speech recognition section you choose: Always (default) saves waiting time but needs the memory all the time. Automatic keeps the model loaded when your computer has enough memory, otherwise it unloads after 5 minutes. After idle time unloads it after the time you set. When memory runs short, WhisPaste unloads the model automatically and loads it again once there is room.",
  "@manualC01S3B2I3": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC01S3B3": "In the Speech recognition area, the entry “Re-run benchmark” measures how fast each installed tier runs on your computer. The results show on the model cards how much longer a tier takes and determine the recommended Whisper tier. For European languages WhisPaste recommends Parakeet instead. The test does not start during a recording.",
  "manualC02Title": "Recording and pasting",
  "manualC02S1Heading": "The hotkey",
  "manualC02S1B1": "The hotkey is a key combination that works in every program. Default: {k2} on Windows and Linux, {k3} on Mac. You can change it under Settings → Keyboard shortcuts.",
  "@manualC02S1B1": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k2": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k3": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC02S1B2": "If another program already uses the combination, WhisPaste uses {k2} instead for the hotkey (on Mac, {k3}). The other hotkeys stay off until you set a free combination.",
  "@manualC02S1B2": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k2": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k3": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC02S2Heading": "Hold or toggle",
  "manualC02S2B1": "In Settings → Keyboard shortcuts, choose how the hotkey works:",
  "manualC02S2B2I1": "“Hold to record” on: hold the hotkey, speak, and release. Releasing ends the recording.",
  "manualC02S2B2I2": "Off: one press starts the recording, a second press ends it.",
  "manualC02S3Heading": "Seeing the recording",
  "manualC02S3B1": "The dock at the bottom of the main window shows the current state. While recording, the main button changes to “Stop recording”, and the status area shows the current step. The dock is always there and cannot be turned off.",
  "manualC02S3B3": "In a narrow window, the dock moves less important controls into the “More” menu, including the hotkey, the Auto-Paste hint, and the update notice. Everything stays reachable there.",
  "manualC02S3B2I1": "“Recording overlay” set to “Floating (always visible)”: a small waveform overlay above all programs. Default: off.",
  "manualC02S3B2I2": "“Floating button”: a button you click to record. Default: off. On Linux under Wayland, the desktop may limit its position and whether it stays on top.",
  "manualC02S4Heading": "Pasting after recording",
  "manualC02S4B1": "Under “After transcription”, choose what happens after each recording:",
  "manualC02S4B2I1": "“Copy to clipboard” (default): the text goes to the clipboard, and you paste it yourself.",
  "manualC02S4B2I2": "“Auto-Paste at cursor”: WhisPaste pastes the text at the cursor.",
  "manualC02S4B2I3": "“Copy & Auto-Paste”: both.",
  "manualC02S4B2I4": "“Do nothing”: WhisPaste neither copies nor pastes the text.",
  "manualC02S4B3": "Apps on the “Auto-Paste blocklist” get no automatic pasting. The text then goes to the clipboard, or only to Recordings if “Copy to the clipboard when apps are blocked” is off. Enter one app per line in the field. If a paste fails, WhisPaste shows a notice and the text stays on the clipboard.",
  "manualC02S4B4": "On Windows, auto-paste does not work in programs running with administrator rights.",
  "manualC02S4B5": "On Linux, WhisPaste marks the text with a hint that only KDE's Klipper honours. Other clipboard managers such as GPaste or CopyQ also store your transcripts: turn off their clipboard recording or delete the entry there.",
  "manualC02S4B6": "After pasting, WhisPaste normally puts back what was on your clipboard before. Under “Clipboard after pasting” you can choose “Keep the transcript” instead: then the transcript stays on the clipboard. If a paste cannot be confirmed in time, the transcript always stays there. If macOS denies access to the clipboard, WhisPaste cannot keep the previous content and does not restore it; the transcript then stays on the clipboard. Once, a hint shows the way to System Settings.",
  "@manualC02S4B5": {
    "description": "Linux clipboard history: only KDE Klipper honours the hint; other clipboard managers still record transcripts."
  },
  "manualC03Title": "Quick note",
  "manualC03S1Heading": "What the quick note does",
  "manualC03S1B1": "The quick note is a note that WhisPaste appends new recordings to. This lets you collect thoughts or a list without creating a new note each time.",
  "manualC03S1B2": "If no note is marked yet, WhisPaste creates a new one the first time and marks it.",
  "manualC03S2Heading": "Setting it up",
  "manualC03S2B1I1": "Open the note in the Notes area and turn on “Make this the quick note the hotkey appends to”. “Quick note — remove the mark” removes the mark.",
  "manualC03S2B1I2": "Turn on the quick-note hotkey under Settings → Keyboard shortcuts. It is off by default. The key is {k1} ({k2}, or {k3} on Mac).",
  "@manualC03S2B1I2": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k2": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k3": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC04Title": "Smart Mode",
  "manualC04S1Heading": "What Smart Mode does",
  "manualC04S1B1": "{k1} edits the recognized text before it is pasted. It is off by default; you turn it on yourself.",
  "@manualC04S1B1": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC04S1B2": "By default, processing runs on your device (“Locally on device”). With “OpenAI”, the text is sent to OpenAI. The privacy chapter has the details.",
  "manualC04S2Heading": "Presets",
  "manualC04S2B1": "A preset decides what happens to the text:",
  "manualC04S2B2I1": "“Off”: no post-processing; the text stays as it was recognized.",
  "manualC04S2B2I2": "“Cleanup”: removes filler words such as “um” and fixes punctuation and capitalization, without changing the wording, meaning, or language.",
  "manualC04S2B2I3": "“Concise”: removes repetition and filler, keeps every important fact and the language.",
  "manualC04S2B2I4": "“Translate”: translates the text into the target language you set.",
  "manualC04S3Heading": "Target language and hotkey",
  "manualC04S3B1": "For “Translate”, choose a target language: German, English, Spanish, French, Portuguese, Mandarin, or Russian. The default is English.",
  "manualC04S3B2": "A separate hotkey for {k1} is off by default. It uses the preset and target language from the settings.",
  "@manualC04S3B2": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC04S4Heading": "Resources",
  "manualC04S4B1": "The local variant downloads a text model of about {size}. If your device has less than {ram} of RAM, WhisPaste warns before the download, but you can still download. While running, the text model needs an extra 4 to 5 GB of RAM.",
  "manualC04S4B2": "While no text model is set up (local model not downloaded, or no OpenAI key for OpenAI), all presets except “Off” are locked. The dock and Settings name the reason and lead you to the download or the key. If post-processing still fails, WhisPaste says so and tells you whether the unedited text was pasted or is only on the clipboard.",
  "manualC05Title": "Dictionary",
  "manualC05S1Heading": "How replacements work",
  "manualC05S1B1": "A replacement automatically swaps certain words or phrases for other text in every recording.",
  "manualC05S1B2": "Each replacement has one or more trigger phrases, the phrases to look for, and the new text. Enter several trigger phrases for the same text under “Trigger phrases”.",
  "manualC05S2Heading": "Matching",
  "manualC05S2B1I1": "Exact: only the identical spelling is replaced.",
  "manualC05S2B1I2": "Similar: slightly different spellings are replaced too. This applies only to trigger phrases of at least 4 characters.",
  "manualC05S2B1I3": "Tolerance (strict, standard, or tolerant): set per entry, not for all entries at once.",
  "manualC05S3Heading": "Import and export (CSV)",
  "manualC05S3B1": "You can back up or transfer your replacements as a CSV file. The file has the columns {k1}. Separate several trigger phrases with {k2}. A file can be at most {k3} and {k4} lines.",
  "manualC05S3B2": "Import and export are in the More menu (⋯) above the list. The try-it field opens from the same menu.",
  "@manualC05S3B1": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k2": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k3": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k4": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC06Title": "Snippets",
  "manualC06S1Heading": "What snippets are",
  "manualC06S1B1": "A snippet is a block of text you insert with a trigger word or a hotkey, such as a signature or a standard reply.",
  "manualC06S1B2I1": "“Static”: the text is inserted exactly as you saved it.",
  "manualC06S1B2I2": "“Interactive”: WhisPaste asks for individual fields one after another by recording, and places them in your template.",
  "manualC06S2Heading": "Opening the snippet picker",
  "manualC06S2B1": "There are two ways to open the picker:",
  "manualC06S2B2I1": "With the picker trigger word: say only this word. It counts only if the whole recording is exactly this word. You set it in Settings under Keyboard shortcuts, group Notes & snippets, right below the picker hotkey. Leave it empty to turn the picker off.",
  "manualC06S2B2I2": "With the picker hotkey: off by default; turn it on under “Picker hotkey”.",
  "manualC06S3Heading": "Creating a snippet",
  "manualC06S3B1I1": "Create a snippet with “Add” and choose “Static” or “Interactive”.",
  "manualC06S3B1I2": "For “Interactive”, define the fields and write the template. Put placeholders in double curly braces, such as {k1}.",
  "@manualC06S3B1I2": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC07Title": "Notes",
  "manualC07S1Heading": "Working with notes",
  "manualC07S1B1": "The Notes area collects text, such as ideas or research. Recordings go straight into a note when you use the quick note.",
  "manualC07S1B2I1": "“Mark as favorite” highlights a note.",
  "manualC07S1B2I2": "“Add tag” assigns a note to a category.",
  "manualC07S2Heading": "Trash",
  "manualC07S2B1": "“Move to trash” puts a note in the trash. It stays there until you delete it for good. The trash is never emptied automatically.",
  "manualC07S2B2I1": "“Delete forever” removes the note from the trash.",
  "manualC07S3Heading": "Quick note",
  "manualC07S3B1": "The Notes area shows which note is the quick note. Details are in the quick note chapter.",
  "manualC07S4Heading": "Images and privacy",
  "manualC07S4B1": "When you add an image, WhisPaste removes metadata such as the location (GPS), camera data, and EXIF, XMP and IPTC information. Only the cleaned copy is stored.",
  "notesPinGateTitle": "Notes are locked",
  "notesPinGateHint": "Enter your PIN to show your notes.",
  "manualC08Title": "Recordings",
  "manualC08S1Heading": "What recordings hold",
  "manualC08S1B1": "Recordings shows every entry: the recognized text, with its date. If audio was saved, the audio file belongs to that entry.",
  "manualC08S2Heading": "Search and filter",
  "manualC08S2B1I1": "Type {k1} to filter by tags.",
  "@manualC08S2B1I1": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC08S2B1I2": "Type {k1} and a language to filter by language.",
  "@manualC08S2B1I2": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC08S2B1I3": "Or just type a keyword.",
  "manualC08S2B1I4": "Above the list are the filters “Favorites”, “Archived”, “Trash”, and “All”.",
  "manualC08S3Heading": "Managing entries",
  "manualC08S3B1I1": "“Copy text” copies the text to the clipboard again.",
  "manualC08S3B1I2": "“Add to favorites” keeps an entry at the top. “Remove from favorites” undoes that.",
  "manualC08S3B1I3": "“Archive” moves an entry out of the main list without deleting it.",
  "manualC08S3B1I4": "“Duplicate”, “Merge” (several entries into one), and “Select multiple” help you tidy up.",
  "manualC08S3B1I5": "“Add annotation” and “Add tag…” add details to an entry.",
  "manualC08S4Heading": "Voice note",
  "manualC08S4B1": "Start a voice note on the entry. Say “tag: name” to set a tag, or “correct: text” to replace the entry’s text.",
  "manualC08S4B2": "A correction replaces the entry’s whole text, not just one word. “korrektur: text” works the same way. Right afterwards you can undo the change from the notice.",
  "manualC08S5Heading": "PIN protection",
  "manualC08S5B1": "With “PIN protection”, a PIN is required before recordings are shown. This also applies to the side panel, the menu of the floating button, and the automation API. The PIN keeps others from casually viewing your transcriptions, but it does not encrypt them. Notes are locked the same way. With a PIN set, the tray menu lists recent recordings by time and word count instead of their first words.",
  "manualC08S5B2": "A forgotten PIN cannot be recovered. To reset it, all transcriptions and saved audio files (including archive and trash), all notes with their versions, and all note images are deleted immediately. Settings, snippets, and replacements are kept.",
  "manualC08S5B3": "While the recordings are locked by a PIN, the clipboard tab in the side panel shows no copied text and pastes none. Copied text comes back once you unlock them.",
  "manualC08S6Heading": "Automatic emptying",
  "manualC08S6B1": "Under “Auto-delete trash after”, set how long deleted entries stay in the trash before they are removed automatically.",
  "manualC09Title": "Importing audio files",
  "manualC09S1Heading": "Transcribing audio files",
  "manualC09S1B1": "You can have existing audio files transcribed. Choose “{k1}” and pick the file.",
  "@manualC09S1B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC09S1B2": "Besides {k1}, you can import more formats depending on your system: on Mac {k2}, on Linux {k3}, on Windows {k4}.",
  "@manualC09S1B2": {
    "placeholders": {
      "k1": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k2": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k3": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "k4": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "manualC09S2Heading": "Limits",
  "manualC09S2B2": "What to do: split the recording into shorter parts and import them one by one.",
  "manualC09S3Heading": "Import errors",
  "manualC09S3B2": "What to do: try again. If that does not help, restart WhisPaste or choose another model under {k1}.",
  "@manualC09S3B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC10Title": "Statistics",
  "manualC10S1Heading": "The areas",
  "manualC10S1B1": "The statistics have three areas: {k1}, {k2}, and {k3}.",
  "@manualC10S1B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}, "k3": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC10S1B2": "Use {k1} and {k2} to choose the time range.",
  "@manualC10S1B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC10S2Heading": "What the numbers mean",
  "manualC10S2B1I1": "{k1} and {k2} count your recordings and how long you recorded.",
  "@manualC10S2B1I1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC10S2B1I2": "{k1} is a rough estimate: WhisPaste counts two thirds of the recording time as saved, because speaking is usually faster than typing. It is not a measurement.",
  "@manualC10S2B1I2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC10S2B1I3": "{k1}: local recordings save cloud costs. WhisPaste estimates this at {k2} per minute, a fixed reference rate.",
  "@manualC10S2B1I3": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC10S3Heading": "Reset",
  "manualC10S3B1": "“{k1}” deletes all statistics data. WhisPaste asks first, and this cannot be undone.",
  "@manualC10S3B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11Title": "Settings",
  "manualC11S1Heading": "The sections",
  "manualC11S1B1": "Settings are grouped into sections. The most important ones:",
  "manualC11S1B2I1": "{k1}: how the app looks.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I2": "{k1}: model and recognition language.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I3": "{k1}: microphone and volume.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I3": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I4": "{k1}: preset, target language, and provider.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I4": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I5": "{k1}: what happens after a recording.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I5": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I6": "{k1}: hotkeys.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I6": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I7": "{k1}: trash period.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I7": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I8": "{k1}: export, import, and automatic backup.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I8": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I9": "{k1}: local API and event hooks for programs on this computer.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I9": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I10": "{k1}: more options, such as reset.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I10": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S1B2I11": "{k1}: version, update check, links, and licences.",
  "@manualC11S1B2I11": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S2Heading": "Back up and reset",
  "manualC11S2B1I1": "{k1} saves your settings automatically after changes. The last five files are kept. It is off by default.",
  "@manualC11S2B1I1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC11S2B1I2": "{k1} immediately deletes all transcriptions, audio files and settings and resets WhisPaste. Read the confirmation carefully before you confirm.",
  "@manualC11S2B1I2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC12Title": "Privacy and offline use",
  "manualC12S1Heading": "What stays on your device",
  "manualC12S1B1": "By default, speech recognition runs on your device. Audio goes to a cloud service only when you actively choose a cloud provider. Transcriptions are stored in a local database on your device, and saved audio files as files next to it. The audio of your last {count} recordings is kept only while “{k1}” is on, and for {days} days at most.",
  "@manualC12S1B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "count": {"type": "int"}, "days": {"type": "int"}}},
  "manualC12S1B2": "The update check asks GitHub for new versions. Feedback is sent only when you submit it.",
  "manualC12S1B3": "If a transcription fails because the server or the connection is not available, the audio of that recording is kept for up to 24 hours, so you can try again from the error message or under Privacy. This also applies when audio retention is off. If it is on, the normal retention applies instead.",
  "@manualC12S1B3": {"description": "Handbook paragraph on the audio of a failed transcription, kept for a retry for up to 24 hours."},
  "manualC12S2Heading": "Cloud providers",
  "manualC12S2B1": "The providers OpenAI and Deepgram need your own API key. Enter it under {k1}.",
  "@manualC12S2B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC12S3Heading": "Usage statistics and error reports",
  "manualC12S3B1": "Two options are on by default: {k1} and {k2}. You can turn both off in {k3}.",
  "@manualC12S3B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}, "k3": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC13Title": "Hardware and performance",
  "manualC13S1Heading": "Memory",
  "manualC13S1B1": "WhisPaste recommends at least {k1} of memory. With less, the app still starts and recommends the “Fast” speech model.",
  "@manualC13S1B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC13S2Heading": "Graphics card",
  "manualC13S2B1": "WhisPaste uses the graphics card when it can speed up speech recognition:",
  "manualC13S2B2I1": "{k1}: {k2}, Apple’s graphics interface.",
  "@manualC13S2B2I1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC13S2B2I2": "{k1} and {k2} with AMD or Intel graphics: {k3}, a widely used graphics interface.",
  "@manualC13S2B2I2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}, "k3": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC13S2B2I3": "NVIDIA cards also use {k1}. With the optional CUDA pack, recognition also uses {k2}.",
  "@manualC13S2B2I3": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC13S2B2I4": "Without a suitable graphics card, WhisPaste computes on the processor ({k1}). That is slower.",
  "@manualC13S2B2I4": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC13S3Heading": "The CUDA pack",
  "manualC13S3B1": "The CUDA pack is an optional add-on for NVIDIA cards, per the app for {k1} and {k2}. It is available for {k3} and {k4} (x64). Turn it on under {k5}.",
  "@manualC13S3B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}, "k3": {"type": "String"}, "k4": {"type": "String"}, "k5": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC13S3B2": "The download is one-time. The app shows its size.",
  "manualC13S3B3": "The pack contains NVIDIA components. Before the first download you accept the NVIDIA CUDA licence (version 2026-01-26); the consent applies to this installation. Without a valid consent the row shows “Consent required”, and WhisPaste uses Vulkan or the CPU until you accept. If the licence text or the pack changes, you are asked again.",
  "manualC13S4Heading": "Graphics acceleration",
  "manualC13S4B1": "Under {k1}, choose whether WhisPaste uses the graphics card. Processor only is usually slower.",
  "@manualC13S4B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC13S5Heading": "Models and size",
  "manualC13S5B1": "The Whisper models come in three tiers: Fast, Balanced, and Accurate. More accurate tiers usually recognise better but need more processing time.",
  "manualC14Title": "Troubleshooting",
  "manualC14S1Heading": "How to read this page",
  "manualC14S1B1": "Each section starts with a notice WhisPaste shows. The wording is the app’s own text. Below it are the cause and the next step.",
  "manualC14S2Heading": "No microphone access",
  "manualC14S2B2": "What to do: allow WhisPaste microphone access in your system settings. Then start the recording again.",
  "manualC14S3Heading": "No microphone found",
  "manualC14S3B2": "What to do: connect a microphone and choose it under {k1}.",
  "@manualC14S3B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S4Heading": "No audio captured",
  "manualC14S4B2": "What to do: check that the right microphone is selected and the {k1} is not at zero. Then record again.",
  "@manualC14S4B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S5Heading": "No speech model",
  "manualC14S5B2": "What to do: download a model under {k1}, then try again.",
  "@manualC14S5B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S6Heading": "Unknown model",
  "manualC14S6B2": "What to do: choose an installed model under {k1}.",
  "@manualC14S6B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S7Heading": "Transcription failed",
  "manualC14S7B2": "What to do: try again. If that does not help, restart WhisPaste or choose another model under {k1}.",
  "@manualC14S7B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S8Heading": "No text recognized",
  "manualC14S8B2": "What to do: speak more clearly or a little longer and try again. Also check the microphone.",
  "manualC14S9Heading": "Recording or transcription too long",
  "manualC14S9B2": "What to do: record shorter sections.",
  "manualC14S10Heading": "Cloud key missing or invalid",
  "manualC14S10B2": "What to do: enter the key again under {k1}, or switch to on-device recognition.",
  "@manualC14S10B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S11Heading": "Graphics memory full",
  "manualC14S11B2": "What to do: nothing. You can choose the model again later in Settings.",
  "manualC14S12Heading": "Calculated on the processor",
  "manualC14S12B2": "What to do: usually nothing. If it happens often, check the setting under {k1} and update the graphics driver.",
  "@manualC14S12B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S13Heading": "Auto-Paste blocked (macOS)",
  "manualC14S13B2": "What to do: allow WhisPaste accessibility access in the system settings. If the message stays, restart WhisPaste.",
  "manualC14S14Heading": "Auto-Paste blocked (Windows)",
  "manualC14S14B2": "What to do: start WhisPaste as an administrator too.",
  "manualC14S15Heading": "Auto-Paste on Linux",
  "@manualC14S15Heading": {
    "description": "Heading of handbook chapter 14, section 15: auto-paste on Linux."
  },
  "manualC14S15B1": "On Linux, auto-paste uses a virtual input device (uinput). If it does not work, check whether WhisPaste may access that device.",
  "@manualC14S15B1": {
    "description": "Explains that auto-paste on Linux uses a virtual input device (uinput), and what to check when it does not work."
  },
  "manualC14S15B2": "The .deb package grants no access when it is installed. Auto-paste asks first: in the setup or under Settings → After transcription, choose “Allow (administrator password)” and enter your administrator password. While the permission is in place, other programs in your session can create key presses too. “Remove permission” takes it back at any time; uninstalling removes it as well.",
  "@manualC14S15B2": {
    "description": "The .deb flow (R-02): nothing is granted on install; the user allows /dev/uinput in the app with the administrator password and can remove it again."
  },
  "manualC14S15B3": "The Flatpak build gives the app access to the system's input devices so that auto-paste can work. WhisPaste itself does not read input devices.",
  "@manualC14S15B3": {
    "description": "Flatpak note: what the sandbox permission gives the app. Plain language, no technical flags."
  },
  "manualC14S15B4": "In the Snap build, run this once in a terminal:",
  "@manualC14S15B4": {
    "description": "Lead-in before the Snap command; the command itself follows in its own copyable block."
  },
  "manualC14S15B5": "The AppImage needs access to /dev/uinput. In the setup or in the settings, copy the command and run it once in a terminal. It installs the udev rule 71-whispaste-uinput.rules into /etc/udev/rules.d/, which gives write access only to the signed-in session. Until then, auto-paste only copies the text.",
  "@manualC14S15B5": {
    "description": "AppImage setup: the copied udev command (session access only) and what happens until setup is done."
  },
  "manualC14S15TerminalHeading": "Terminals and Wayland",
  "@manualC14S15TerminalHeading": {"description": "Handbook troubleshooting heading: terminal paste shortcut under Wayland."},
  "manualC14S15T1": "On Linux, terminals paste with Ctrl+Shift+V. WhisPaste recognises common terminals and uses that shortcut there on its own: under X11 and XWayland, and on KDE Plasma, Sway, Hyprland, niri, labwc, Wayfire and other wlroots desktops.",
  "@manualC14S15T1": {"description": "Handbook: Linux terminals paste with Ctrl+Shift+V; where WhisPaste recognises them on its own."},
  "manualC14S15T2": "Under GNOME with Wayland, WhisPaste identifies the target app only with the optional WhisPaste extension for GNOME. Without it, WhisPaste does not recognise terminals, and a block list only copies the text.",
  "@manualC14S15T2": {"description": "Handbook: GNOME Wayland needs the optional WhisPaste GNOME extension to identify the target app."},
  "manualC14S15T3": "If a terminal still shows ^V instead of the text, turn on “{k1}” under {k2}. WhisPaste then pastes with Ctrl+Shift+V everywhere. Some apps use these keys for something else; LibreOffice, for example, opens a dialog.",
  "@manualC14S15T3": {"description": "Handbook: fallback switch. {k1} = the switch title, {k2} = the settings section name.", "placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S15T4": "Under GNOME, turn on the WhisPaste extension in the settings with {k1}. The .deb package already installs it. With Flatpak, AppImage or the tarball, install it once with the script from the unpacked Linux package, then turn it on:",
  "@manualC14S15T4": {"description": "Handbook: how to install and turn on the GNOME extension. {k1} = the button label.", "placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S15InstallExtCmd": "bash install-gnome-extension.sh",
  "@manualC14S15InstallExtCmd": {"description": "Terminal command, not translated."},
  "manualC14S15EnableExtCmd": "gnome-extensions enable whispaste-focus@whispaste.de",
  "@manualC14S15EnableExtCmd": {"description": "Terminal command, not translated."},
  "manualC14S15T5": "Without uinput set up, for example in Flatpak, WhisPaste pastes through desktop permission: {k1} under {k2}. Your desktop asks once; you can withdraw the permission there at any time",
  "@manualC14S15T5": {"description": "Handbook: portal paste without uinput. {k1} = button label, {k2} = settings section name.", "placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "settingsDesktopShortcutGnome": "This desktop does not let apps use system-wide shortcuts yet. WhisPaste can add {shortcut} to the GNOME keyboard shortcuts instead.",
  "@settingsDesktopShortcutGnome": {"description": "Linux Wayland without the GlobalShortcuts portal (GNOME before 48): notice under the hotkey. {shortcut} = the hotkey as key caps text, e.g. Ctrl+Shift+D. Keep GNOME untranslated.", "placeholders": {"shortcut": {"type": "String"}}},
  "settingsDesktopShortcutAdd": "Add to GNOME",
  "settingsDesktopShortcutInstalled": "{shortcut} is set up in the GNOME keyboard shortcuts. If you change the hotkey, WhisPaste updates it there.",
  "@settingsDesktopShortcutInstalled": {"description": "Shown once WhisPaste added its hotkey to the GNOME keyboard shortcuts. {shortcut} = the hotkey, e.g. Ctrl+Shift+D.", "placeholders": {"shortcut": {"type": "String"}}},
  "settingsDesktopShortcutRemove": "Remove from GNOME",
  "settingsDesktopShortcutFailed": "The GNOME keyboard shortcuts could not be changed.",
  "settingsDesktopShortcutManual": "This desktop does not let apps use system-wide shortcuts. Assign this command to a key combination in your system settings:",
  "@settingsDesktopShortcutManual": {"description": "Linux Wayland desktops without the GlobalShortcuts portal where WhisPaste cannot add the shortcut itself (e.g. Sway, Flatpak). A command follows below the text."},
  "manualC14S15HotkeyHeading": "Hotkey under Wayland",
  "manualC14S15H1": "Under Wayland, an app gets system-wide shortcuts only through the desktop. KDE Plasma and GNOME 48 or newer provide them. Older GNOME versions, such as in Ubuntu 24.04, cannot: WhisPaste then offers “{k1}” under {k2} and adds the hotkey to the GNOME keyboard shortcuts.",
  "@manualC14S15H1": {"description": "Handbook: hotkey under Wayland. {k1} = the button label “Add to GNOME”, {k2} = settings section name.", "placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S15H2": "On other desktops, such as Sway or Hyprland, assign the command to a key combination yourself. Settings shows the exact command for your installation under {k1}.",
  "@manualC14S15H2": {"description": "Handbook: manual shortcut on other Wayland desktops. {k1} = settings section name.", "placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S15H3": "If the hotkey does not work in other apps, Settings and onboarding show a notice with the reason, the command for your own key combination, and a “Reconnect” button that asks the desktop again.",
  "manualC14S15G1": "Hold or tap: Hold the key longer than the threshold (default 250 ms) and it works like push-to-talk. A short tap starts and stops a recording.",
  "manualC14S15G2": "Doppeltippen: Unter den Tastenoptionen legst du eine eigene Aktion für Doppeltippen fest, etwa Freihändig, Schnellnotiz oder Snippet-Auswahl. Der zweite Tipp muss innerhalb von 400 ms erfolgen.",
  "manualC14S15G3": "Einzeltaste: Die rechte Strg-, rechte Alt- oder rechte Befehl-Taste bzw. Fn kann allein als Diktiertaste dienen. Auf dem Mac fragt WhisPaste vorher nach der Berechtigung zur Tastatur-Überwachung. Unter Linux mit Wayland ist das nicht verfügbar. On the Mac, the suggested key is Fn. The Globe key does nothing in WhisPaste.",
  "@manualC14S15H3": {"description": "Handbook: what the Wayland hotkey notice offers. “{r}” = the Reconnect button label."},
  "manualC14S15FlatpakHeading": "Flatpak",
  "@manualC14S15FlatpakHeading": {
    "description": "Subheading for the Flatpak build, a Linux app package format. Keep the name as is."
  },
  "manualC14S15B3W": "With this access, the app could in theory read keystrokes of other programs if your user can read the input devices (e.g. as a member of the input group). Members of the input group can also generate virtual input.",
  "@manualC14S15B3W": {
    "description": "Security warning about access to input devices in the Flatpak build."
  },
  "manualC14S15B3S": "Auto-paste also needs write access to /dev/uinput on the host. Install the udev rule 71-whispaste-uinput.rules into /etc/udev/rules.d/ and then run these commands:",
  "@manualC14S15B3S": {
    "description": "Lead-in before the udev command block (Flatpak). The commands follow in their own copyable block."
  },
  "manualC14S15Cmd": "sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=misc --sysname-match=uinput",
  "@manualC14S15Cmd": {
    "description": "Shell command shown in a copyable block. Keep the command unchanged."
  },
  "manualCodeCopy": "Copy command",
  "@manualCodeCopy": {
    "description": "Label of the copy button next to a command block, also its tooltip. Use the same wording as pasteFailureLinuxUinputCopy."
  },
  "manualCodeCopied": "Command copied",
  "@manualCodeCopied": {
    "description": "Confirmation toast after a command has been copied to the clipboard."
  },
  "manualCodeCopyFailed": "Could not copy. Select the command and copy it by hand.",
  "manualC14S15B3E": "The rule gives write access only to the signed-in session. These commands need administrator rights (sudo) and change the system. If you do not want this, leave auto-paste off and paste the text by hand. To remove the rule, use the button in the settings that copies the matching command.",
  "@manualC14S15B3E": {
    "description": "Warning that the udev rule gives write access to the signed-in session only, that the commands need administrator rights, and how to remove the rule."
  },
  "manualC14S15SnapHeading": "Snap",
  "@manualC14S15SnapHeading": {
    "description": "Subheading for the Snap build, a Linux app package format. Keep the name as is."
  },
  "manualC14S15SnapCmd": "sudo snap connect whispaste:uinput",
  "@manualC14S15SnapCmd": {
    "description": "Shell command for the Snap build. Keep the command unchanged."
  },
  "manualC14S15Fallback": "Until then, auto-paste only copies the text.",
  "@manualC14S15Fallback": {
    "description": "Sentence after the setup options: until setup is done, auto-paste only copies the text."
  },
  "manualC14S15AppImageHeading": "AppImage",
  "@manualC14S15AppImageHeading": {
    "description": "Subheading for the AppImage build, a Linux app package format. Keep the name as is."
  },
  "manualC14S16Heading": "Hotkey already in use",
  "manualC14S16B2": "What to do: choose a different combination under {k1}.",
  "@manualC14S16B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S17Heading": "Autostart not set up",
  "manualC14S17B2": "What to do: check the autostart permissions in your operating system. Without autostart, WhisPaste does not start on its own.",
  "manualC14S18Heading": "Automatic backup failed",
  "manualC14S18B2": "What to do: choose a different, reachable folder under {k1}.",
  "@manualC14S18B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S19Heading": "Factory reset incomplete",
  "manualC14S19B2": "What to do: choose “Try again”, or restart WhisPaste and run the reset again afterwards.",
  "manualC14S20Heading": "No sound detected",
  "manualC14S20B2": "What to do: check the microphone under {k1} and then record again.",
  "@manualC14S20B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC14S21Heading": "Not enough memory",
  "manualC14S21B1": "WhisPaste still starts with less memory than the recommended {k1}. The app then recommends the “Fast” speech model.",
  "@manualC14S21B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15Title": "Keyboard shortcuts",
  "manualC15S1Heading": "Only inside WhisPaste",
  "manualC15S1B1": "These keyboard shortcuts work only while the WhisPaste window is active. The system-wide hotkey, by contrast, is set under {k2}.",
  "@manualC15S1B1": {"placeholders": {"k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S1B2": "On Mac, {k1} usually replaces {k2}.",
  "@manualC15S1B2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S1B3I1": "F1 opens help.",
  "@manualC15S1B3I1": {"description": "Shortcut reference: the F1 key opens help."},
  "manualC15S1B3I2": "{k} opens help as well.",
  "@manualC15S1B3I2": {"description": "Shortcut reference: the platform chord {k} also opens help.", "placeholders": {"k": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S2Heading": "Recordings",
  "manualC15S2B1I1": "{k1}: delete the entry.",
  "@manualC15S2B1I1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S2B1I2": "{k1}: toggle favorite.",
  "@manualC15S2B1I2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S2B1I3": "{k1}: search.",
  "@manualC15S2B1I3": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S2B1I4": "{k1}: close search or the detail view.",
  "@manualC15S2B1I4": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S2B1I5": "{k1}: copy the entry.",
  "@manualC15S2B1I5": {"description": "Handbuch Kap. 15, Aufnahmen: Enter copies the focused entry. {k1} is the key name.", "placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S2B1I6": "{k1}: discard an edit. Unsaved changes ask first.",
  "@manualC15S2B1I6": {"description": "Handbuch Kap. 15, Aufnahmen: Esc in the transcript editor discards the edit; unsaved changes ask first. {k1} is the key name.", "placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S3Heading": "Notes",
  "manualC15S3B1I1": "{k1}: delete the entry.",
  "@manualC15S3B1I1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S3B1I2": "{k1}: create a new note.",
  "@manualC15S3B1I2": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S3B1I3": "{k1}: search.",
  "@manualC15S3B1I3": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S4Heading": "Dictionary and snippets",
  "manualC15S4B1I1": "{k1}: delete the entry.",
  "@manualC15S4B1I1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC15S5Heading": "Cancel during a recording",
  "@manualC15S5Heading": {"description": "Manual heading: cancelling a dictation with Esc, which is caught system-wide while a recording runs (UIA-SHL-14)."},
  "manualC15S5B1": "While a recording or transcription runs, WhisPaste catches the {k1} key system-wide so you can cancel. {k1} then does nothing in other apps. If that bothers you, choose {k2} as the cancel key in Settings.",
  "@manualC15S5B1": {"description": "Manual paragraph: while a recording or transcription runs, WhisPaste catches the cancel key ({k1}, Esc) system-wide; {k2} (F12) is the alternative to choose in Settings (UIA-SHL-14).", "placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC16Title": "Feedback and support",
  "manualC16S1Heading": "Sending feedback",
  "manualC16S1B1I1": "Rating: required.",
  "manualC16S1B1I2": "Type: required. Choose Problem, Idea, Praise, or Question.",
  "manualC16S1B1I3": "Free text up to 1000 characters.",
  "manualC16S1B1I4": "An email address is optional.",
  "manualC16S1B2": "If you have sent feedback recently, the app shows this notice:",
  "manualC16S2Heading": "Support",
  "manualC16S2B1": "The {k1} tab on the Help page shows how you can support WhisPaste.",
  "@manualC16S2B1": {"placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}}},
  "manualC16S3Heading": "Rating reminder",
  "@manualC16S3Heading": {"description": "Handbook heading: rating reminder and how to lift a 'Never ask again' choice."},
  "manualC16S3B1": "If you chose “Never ask again” for the rating reminder, you find the switch “{k2}” under {k1}. It appears only in that case.",
  "manualC16S4B1": "You can send feedback from the Help tab, from the Help menu in the menu bar (macOS) or the title-bar menu (Windows and Linux), and from the tray. The form is two steps away.",
  "manualC16S5Heading": "Share an idea",
  "manualC16S5B1": "Choose Idea, or open Suggest an idea from the Help menu: the type is already set. You can also post your idea on the public ideas board and vote on others.",
  "manualC16S6Heading": "Write by voice",
  "manualC16S6B1": "The microphone button in the message field records your voice and inserts the recognized text at the cursor.",
  "manualC16S7Heading": "What is sent",
  "manualC16S7B1I1": "The type you chose and your message.",
  "manualC16S7B1I3": "Your e-mail address only if you entered one. It is used only for a reply and deleted after 90 days.",
  "manualC16S7B1I4": "Diagnostics only if you turn on Attach diagnostics: app version, operating system, speech engine and backend. Show preview displays the exact text before you send.",
  "manualC16S7B1I5": "Only for Praise: the consent to show your praise as a quote on the website. It is off by default and you can withdraw it with one click on this page.",
  "manualC16S7B2": "Recordings and transcripts are never attached.",
  "manualC16S4Heading": "Where to find the form",
  "manualC16S7B1I2": "The rating you chose.",
  "@manualC16S3B1": {"description": "Handbook paragraph: where the switch that lifts 'Never ask again' is. {k1} is the Interface area, {k2} the switch label.", "placeholders": {"k1": {"type": "String"}, "k2": {"type": "String"}}},
  "pasteFailureClipboardCopy": "Could not paste – the text is on the clipboard ({paste}).",
  "pasteFailureCheckPermission": "Check permission",
  "autoPasteResetConfirmTitle": "Reset entry and allow again?",
  "autoPasteResetConfirmBody": "macOS stored an old entry for WhisPaste that no longer applies. WhisPaste removes only this Accessibility entry. macOS will then ask you again. Other permissions stay unchanged.",
  "autoPasteResetConfirmButton": "Reset entry and allow again",
  "permissionRowMicTitle": "Microphone",
