  "manualProfilesTitle": "Profiles and quick switching",
  "manualProfilesS1Heading": "Creating profiles",
  "manualProfilesS1Body": "A profile is a named set of recording settings. Create it under Settings → Profiles and decide for each field whether the profile sets it or leaves it unchanged.",
  "manualProfilesS1B1": "Speech model, language, Smart Mode, after-transcription action and microphone",
  "manualProfilesS1B2": "Up to 9 profiles. Every field can be set to “Leave unchanged”.",
  "manualProfilesS2Heading": "Hotkeys",
  "manualProfilesS2Body": "Each profile can have its own hotkey. Pressing it activates the profile, and it stays active until you choose another one or change one of its fields by hand.",
  "manualProfilesS2Tip": "A hotkey needs a modifier key. A combination that another feature already uses stays inactive, and the profile shows it as a conflict.",
  "manualProfilesS3Heading": "Automatic per app",
  "manualProfilesS3Body": "If you add an app under target apps, the profile becomes active whenever that app is in front while you dictate. The identifier depends on the operating system:",
  "manualProfilesS3Mac": "macOS: bundle ID, for example com.apple.mail",
  "manualProfilesS3Win": "Windows: program name without .exe, for example chrome",
  "manualProfilesS3Linux": "Linux: window WM_CLASS under X11, for example google-chrome. Under Wayland WhisPaste cannot detect the app.",
  "manualProfilesS4Heading": "Tray and overlay",
  "manualProfilesS4Body": "The tray menu has a Profile submenu: “Automatic, by app” follows the rules, “No profile” switches them off, and your profiles are listed below. In the recording overlay, the name of the active profile follows the time and language, for example 0:07 · DE · Mail.",
  "manualProfilesS5Heading": "Leave unchanged",
